 "agentAttributes": [
  {
   "id": "state",
   "name": "state",
   "type": "bool",
   "defaultValue": "false",
   "description": "The node's single bit — the alphabet the census counts and both rule tables are keyed by."
  },
  {
   "id": "prio",
   "name": "prio",
   "type": "float",
   "defaultValue": "1000000",
   "description": "The LATCHED division intent AND its tie-break in one number. The state tick writes it: a flagged node stores its OWN HANDLE (below 100000), an unflagged one stores 1000000. Each of the 8 division rounds that follow splits a node only if its value is below 100000 (still latched) and strictly below every bonded neighbour's (it won the contest); a splitter then writes 1000000, which consumes its latch AND stops it blocking the neighbours it beat, so they split in a later round of the same tick against the adjacency it just rewrote. Handles are unique, so strict inequality always resolves and the splitters of any one round are pairwise non-adjacent — and because the winner is always the LOWEST handle, the drain order is the reference implementation's own ascending index walk rather than a random one. The default is a non-splitter value, so a newborn can never divide in a later round of the tick it was born in."
  }
 ],
